# This Mac

This Mac's setup (command-line tools, apps, dotfiles, macOS settings and
Claude Code's own settings) is managed by chezmoi from the cradle repo, at
`chezmoi source-path` (normally `~/Documents/cradle`).

When asked to install, update, change or remove anything about this machine's
setup, from any folder, read that repo's CLAUDE.md and make the change there.
Don't edit the managed files in `~` directly, and don't install tools
globally with `brew install`, `npm install -g`, `pip install`, `uv tool
install` or `go install`; they belong in the repo's mise config or Brewfile.
Project dependencies inside a project are fine.
{{- if .obsidianVault }}

# Obsidian

The user's Obsidian vault is `{{ .obsidianVault }}`: plain Markdown files that
Obsidian syncs. Read, search and link notes there whenever it helps, from any
project.
{{- $private := list }}
{{- range splitList ";" .obsidianPrivate }}{{ $f := trim . | trimSuffix "/" }}{{ if $f }}{{ $private = append $private $f }}{{ end }}{{ end }}
{{- if $private }}

Never read these folders, with file tools, `grep`, `cat` or any other
command. Claude Code's permissions block its file tools there; shell commands
are kept out only by this rule.
{{- range $private }}
- `{{ . }}`
{{- end }}
{{- end }}

- Write the Obsidian way: `[[wikilinks]]` to other notes, properties (YAML
  frontmatter) where notes use them, attachments where the vault keeps them.
- Add or edit notes when asked, or when a skill says to. Never move, rename or
  delete notes, or change `.obsidian/`, without asking.
- The Daily notes and Templates settings and `Templates/Daily.md` are managed
  from the cradle repo's `obsidian/` folder; change them there, not in the
  vault.
- The `journal` skill writes the day's Claude Code sessions and git commits
  into the daily note; a LaunchAgent runs it every evening at 18:00.
{{- end }}
